  "description": "Operating area:\nSummer (December - April): Sydney Harbour, Pittwater and the Hawkesbury\nAutumn (April - July): Gold Coast and Brisbane\nWinter and spring (July - November): Whitsundays, Cairns, Cooktown and the Ribbon Reefs of the outer Great Barrier Reef\n\nWelcome aboard Shore Thing 115, a 35m (115ft) Lloyds-built luxury superyacht, launched in 1986 and refitted in 2025. Four ensuite cabins, three entertaining decks, a forward deck jacuzzi and a crew that looks after every detail.\n\nShe sleeps up to 8 guests overnight and takes up to 70 guests by day (70 in smooth water, 40 in partially smooth water). Ideal for luxury escapes, special events, corporate charters and sunset cruises.\n\nHighlights: zero-speed stabilisers, Starlink internet and AV, enclosed air-conditioned sky lounge, main deck bar with commercial ice machine, sun deck BBQ and bar, two alfresco dining areas and a 9m Waverider tender.",
